022font-size:14px;\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\u0022\u003ERead For Good is NLB\u0026#39;s signature\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/span\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-size:14px;\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\u0022\u003E reading charity drive\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/span\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-size:14px;\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\u0022\u003E, encouraging reading and sharing the joy of reading with the less privileged. This year\u0026#39;s goal is 500,000 reading sessions (7.5 million reading minutes) during National Reading Month, to bring reading to an estimated community of 10,000 individuals. In 2025, the initiative saw 384,628 participants and raised 3,374 books for beneficiaries.\u003Cbr /\u003E\n\u003Cbr /\u003E\n\u003Cstrong\u003EThe Beneficiaries\u0026nbsp;\u003C/strong\u003E\u003Cbr /\u003E\n\u003Cstrong\u003EkidsREAD\u003C/strong\u003E\u202fis a nationwide reading initiative by NLB in partnership with People\u0026rsquo;s Association, self-help groups, MOE schools and preschools and social service groups to promote the love of reading and cultivate good reading habits among young Singaporeans, specifically children aged 4-8 years old from the less privileged families.\u202f\u202f\u0026nbsp;\u003Cbr /\u003E\n\u003Cbr /\u003E\n\u003Cstrong\u003EMINDS\u202f\u003C/strong\u003Ehas been caring for Persons with Intellectual Disability (PWIDs) and their families since 1962. Grounded in the belief that all PWIDs have innate abilities and talents, MINDS is committed to empowering them and enhancing their quality of life, while advocating for greater inclusivity for PWIDs.\u202f\u202f\u202f\u202f\u0026nbsp;\u003Cbr /\u003E\n\u003Cbr /\u003E\n\u003Cstrong\u003EPreschool Market\u202f\u003C/strong\u003Eis a registered social enterprise committed to\u202fassisting\u202funderprivileged kids and their families. We believe that every child should have equal access to opportunities in learning and\u202feducation, and\u202freaching their maximum potential in life regardless of their socio-economical\u202fstatus. They have received the MSF Community Cares award.\u202f\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\n\n\u003Chr /\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-size:14px;\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\u0022\u003ESMU Libraries are proud to organise this session in support of the initiative, and every minute you spend reading with us counts toward that goal.\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\n\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-size:14px;\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\u0022\u003ESee you there!\u0026nbsp;\ud83d\udc4b\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\n\n\u003Cp style=\u0022margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:16px\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-size:12pt\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022line-height:116%\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\u0022\u003E\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/p\u003E","fromTime":"4:00pm Friday, September 4, 2026","toTime":"5:00pm Friday, September 4, 2026","more_info":"","shortdesc":"Between lectures, deadlines, and projects, when was the last time you read something just for the joy of it?\n\nSMU Libraries are hosting a one-hour mass reading session in support of Read For Good, the...","shortdesc_was_truncated":true,"registration_cost":"","start":"4:00pm","end":"5:00pm","all_day":false,"startdt":"2026-09-04 16:00:00","enddt":"2026-09-04 17:00:00","date":"Friday, September 4, 2026","ymd":"20260904","year":"2026","monthnum":9,"day":"4","daypostfix":"th","dayfull":"Friday","dayshort":"Fri","monthfull":"September","monthshort":"Sep","url":"https://smu-sg.libcal.com/event/5971600","color":"#BEB2F0","locationCount":2,"location":"Learning Lab 3 \u0026 4, Kwa Geok Choo Library Level 3, Quiet Area, L